{"chars": "And how does a greenhouse stay warm at the top of a frozen world? Deep, deep under the sea ice, on the bottom of the Arctic Ocean, there are hot springs where warmth from inside the Earth bubbles up. The elves built a long pipe that carries a little of that warmth up to the greenhouse, so the Earth itself keeps the orchids cozy. In summer, when the sun shines all day and all night at the North Pole, big barrels of water soak up the sunshine and hold on to its warmth for the long winter.", "start": [0.225, 0.225, 0.225, 0.338, 0.338, 0.338, 0.338, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.662, 0.662, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 0.725, 1.2, 1.2, 1.2, 1.2, 1.2, 1.538, 1.538, 1.538, 1.538, 1.538, 1.812, 1.812, 1.812, 1.887, 1.887, 1.887, 1.887, 1.975, 1.975, 1.975, 1.975, 2.188, 2.188, 2.188, 2.263, 2.263, 2.337, 2.337, 2.337, 2.337, 2.337, 2.337, 2.337, 2.775, 2.775, 2.775, 2.775, 2.775, 2.775, 3.525, 3.663, 3.663, 3.663, 3.663, 3.663, 4.1, 4.237, 4.237, 4.237, 4.237, 4.237, 4.463, 4.463, 4.463, 4.463, 4.463, 4.463, 4.638, 4.638, 4.638, 4.638, 4.763, 4.763, 4.763, 4.763, 5.025, 5.025, 5.025, 5.025, 5.525, 5.625, 5.625, 5.625, 5.737, 5.737, 5.737, 5.737, 5.825, 5.825, 5.825, 5.825, 5.825, 5.825, 5.825, 6.112, 6.112, 6.112, 6.188, 6.188, 6.188, 6.188, 6.3, 6.3, 6.3, 6.3, 6.3, 6.3, 6.3, 6.65, 6.65, 6.65, 6.65, 6.65, 6.65, 7.3, 7.4, 7.4, 7.4, 7.4, 7.4, 7.4, 7.525, 7.525, 7.525, 7.525, 7.625, 7.625, 7.625, 7.625, 7.85, 7.85, 7.85, 7.85, 7.85, 7.85, 7.85, 7.85, 8.3, 8.3, 8.3, 8.3, 8.3, 8.3, 8.463, 8.463, 8.463, 8.463, 8.463, 8.463, 8.463, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 8.887, 8.887, 8.887, 8.887, 8.887, 8.887, 8.887, 9.312, 9.312, 9.312, 9.312, 9.45, 9.45, 9.45, 9.45, 9.45, 9.45, 9.725, 9.725, 9.725, 9.725, 9.725, 9.725, 9.725, 9.725, 10.1, 10.1, 10.1, 10.7, 10.8, 10.8, 10.8, 10.8, 10.95, 10.95, 10.95, 10.95, 10.95, 10.95, 11.25, 11.25, 11.25, 11.25, 11.25, 11.25, 11.463, 11.463, 11.525, 11.525, 11.525, 11.525, 11.525, 11.8, 11.8, 11.8, 1